From: mup-2388 <288946382+mup-2388@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:54:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add calendar, to-do, daily brief and email (batch 3)

Real-world assistant features, all stdlib + optional SMTP, wired into both the
agentic tool loop and the offline/Track-1 fast path:

- agenda.py: a small RFC 5545 VEVENT parser + cached fetcher. Reads Google
  Calendar "secret address in iCal format" feeds and Outlook/exported .ics files
  (CALENDAR_ICS_URLS / CALENDAR_ICS_FILES), normalises TZID/floating/UTC times
  to local, and serves agenda(days), next_event() and today().
- tools: calendar_agenda, calendar_next, todo (Markdown list add/list/done/clear),
  daily_brief (date + calendar + to-do + reminders), draft_email (writes the
  draft to notes/drafts/ AND opens Outlook via mailto:, no credentials) and
  send_email (SMTP when SMTP_HOST/USER/PASSWORD are set).
- router: strict schemas + keyword-planner entries for all six tools.
- server: Track-1 regex rules for "what's on my calendar", "good morning",
  "what's on my todo", etc., plus /api/calendar, /api/calendar/next, /api/todo,
  /api/brief.
- apps: "college portal" (CBS_PORTAL_URL) and Google Classroom entries.
- config + .env.example + README: document every new knob.

Named agenda.py (not calendar.py) so the module can never shadow Python's
stdlib calendar, which datetime.strptime imports internally.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
